# Session-Summary-Check - the closing "what shipped / what is left" report.
#
# Copy to .env next to this file and edit. One setting. The one knob
# deliberately NOT offered is an enable/disable flag - see below.
#
# COOLDOWN_MINUTES - minutes before the requirement is delivered again on a
# later prompt of the SAME session. Default 15. SessionStart always delivers
# (a started, resumed, cleared or compacted session is a rebuilt context) and
# stamps the window, so the first prompt after it does not repeat. 0 means
# every prompt.
#
# The requirement is delivered BEFORE the task (SessionStart and
# UserPromptSubmit), never at Stop. On Claude Code a Stop hook's
# additionalContext re-invokes the model, so asking at Stop always cost one
# more assistant turn after the work was already done - "waiting." / "done."
# - which is the loop this hook shipped with twice. Delivered up front, the
# reply that ends the task carries the summary itself, with no extra turn.
COOLDOWN_MINUTES=15

#   * NO ENABLE/DISABLE FLAG. A summary that can be switched off per project
#     is a summary the next session cannot rely on having. Remove the hook if
#     it is genuinely unwanted; do not leave it installed and mute.
#
# The hook reads no project content and writes nothing outside Hook Maker's
# own state directory. It never blocks: a gate that blocks sends the agent
# back to work, and anything it does then lands after the summary, which is
# precisely what this hook is supposed to prevent.
